recommend check-in (Keaton) -- two. THE WALL THAT LANDED REFUSES FOR A PEER'S BREAK: rule six reads the whole index, so one hand's broken living link stops every ship's commit until it is repaired -- which is the fleet-that-cannot-commit risk %524 declined the lap for. The staged-only split is proven buildable and parked on stash@{0}; the choice between reach and blast radius is yours. THE PIER'S OWN CAPACITY: three ships ran full cold roster passes concurrently on four cores this hour and mine took 1,527s cold and 1,304s hot against a nominal 1,139; `--scoped` exists for this and the cold open does not reach for it.
